# f1 = stepOverText
# Nothing is known of what the loop goes over, so it calls the compiler's own library, which makes of a text an object with the text, the place in it and `next`. The two lie under private names of the
# library's own, of the kind that only JavaScript reads and writes: each step asks once whether it was handed that object and then reads two slots. Under a private name of the engine a read never
# takes that road: two calls of a stub for every letter.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key=@#"steppedText"
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key=@#"nextPosition"
# CHECK: = PutSlot {{*}}key=@#"nextPosition"
